From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:43:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] uddf: restore std::cout format after driver log messages

The VB1940 and HSB drivers' log() helpers write to std::cout, and
several callers pass std::hex to print register and FSM state values
without switching back. The stream stays in hex, so the next decimal
output of the application is wrong: nvsipl_camera --validateCrc
prints its CRC summary after the VB1940 StopStreaming message and
reports "CRC validated: 38  Mismatches: 2d" for 56 validated frames
and 45 mismatches.

Save the stream flags on entry to log() and restore them after the
message, so no caller can leave std::cout in hex.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
---
 uddf/drivers/hsb/HsbTransportDriver.cpp | 4 ++++
 uddf/drivers/vb1940/VB1940Module.cpp    | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/uddf/drivers/hsb/HsbTransportDriver.cpp b/uddf/drivers/hsb/HsbTransportDriver.cpp
index e2a001b..90c9362 100644
--- a/uddf/drivers/hsb/HsbTransportDriver.cpp
+++ b/uddf/drivers/hsb/HsbTransportDriver.cpp
@@ -84,9 +84,13 @@ namespace {
 
 template<typename... Args>
 void log(Args... args) {
+    // Callers pass std::hex; restore the stream format so it does not leak
+    // into later std::cout output.
+    const std::ios_base::fmtflags flags = std::cout.flags();
     std::cout << "    [HSB] ";
     (std::cout << ... << args);
     std::cout << std::endl;
+    std::cout.flags(flags);
 }
 
 #define EXTRA_DEBUG 0
diff --git a/uddf/drivers/vb1940/VB1940Module.cpp b/uddf/drivers/vb1940/VB1940Module.cpp
index 2f76d40..8b63c2a 100644
--- a/uddf/drivers/vb1940/VB1940Module.cpp
+++ b/uddf/drivers/vb1940/VB1940Module.cpp
@@ -34,9 +34,13 @@ static constexpr uint8_t SYSTEM_FSM_STATE_STREAMING {0x04U};
 
 template<typename... Args>
 void log(Args... args) {
+    // Callers pass std::hex; restore the stream format so it does not leak
+    // into later std::cout output.
+    const std::ios_base::fmtflags flags = std::cout.flags();
     std::cout << "    [Eagle module] ";
     (std::cout << ... << args);
     std::cout << std::endl;
+    std::cout.flags(flags);
 }
 
 } // Anonymous namespace
